notes:
These are the primary sources the csoh.org kill chain cites. Every fact about the incident in this deck comes from that page, which draws on these.

LiteLLM's security update is the project's own account. PyPI's incident report, whose title names both LiteLLM and Telnyx, gives the exposure time and download figures the page leads with. Cycode, Trend Micro and HeroDevs each wrote up the attack. The MITRE page defines the technique behind stage 01. The page labels the SecurityWeek link as Trivy behind the exposure figures.

The background slides name their own sources, from MITRE ATT&CK and the Kubernetes documentation.

